{"id":"81fa5faf3598651a","group":"58","path":"58/batch13/58-df-parabolic-induction.md","title":"Parabolic Induction","display":"df-parabolic-induction — Parabolic Induction","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-parabolic-induction","aliases":["58-df-parabolic-induction","Parabolic Induction"],"display":"df-parabolic-induction — Parabolic Induction","depends_on":["[[../batch08/58-df-reductive-group.md]]","[[../batch12/58-df-representation.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-parabolic-induction"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-parabolic-induction</span><span>Parabolic Induction</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-parabolic-induction — Parabolic Induction"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"8790321df936a708\" href=\"?note=8790321df936a708\" title=\"../batch08/58-df-reductive-group.md\">../batch08/58-df-reductive-group.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"6f58babd1e46f709\" href=\"?note=6f58babd1e46f709\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-representation.md\">../batch12/58-df-representation.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"G,P,M,N,\\sigma,V_\\sigma,\\pi\\in V\">\\(G,P,M,N,\\sigma,V_\\sigma,\\pi\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P=M\\ltimes N\">\\(P=M\\ltimes N\\)</span> (parabolic subgroup with Levi factor <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M\">\\(M\\)</span> and unipotent radical <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"N\">\\(N\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\delta_P\">\\(\\delta_P\\)</span> (modular character of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P\">\\(P\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Reductive}\">\\(\\operatorname{Reductive}\\)</span> (reductive-group predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"8790321df936a708\" href=\"?note=8790321df936a708\" title=\"../batch08/58-df-reductive-group.md\">../batch08/58-df-reductive-group.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Representation}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Representation}_S\\)</span> (representation predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"6f58babd1e46f709\" href=\"?note=6f58babd1e46f709\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-representation.md\">../batch12/58-df-representation.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ParabolicInduction}_S\\subseteq V^4\">\\(\\mathrm{ParabolicInduction}_S\\subseteq V^4\\)</span> (normalized parabolic-induction predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}parabolic\\text{-}induction} \\vdash \\mathrm{ParabolicInduction}_S(\\pi,G,P,\\sigma)\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{Reductive}(G)\\land P=M\\ltimes N\\land\\mathrm{Representation}_S(\\sigma,M,V_\\sigma)\\land\\pi=\\{f\\in V_\\sigma^G:\\operatorname{Smooth}(f)\\land\\forall m\\in M\\;\\forall n\\in N\\;\\forall g\\in G\\;(f(mng)=\\delta_P(m)^{1/2}\\sigma(m)f(g))\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}parabolic\\text{-}induction} \\vdash \\mathrm{ParabolicInduction}_S(\\pi,G,P,\\sigma)\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{Reductive}(G)\\land P=M\\ltimes N\\land\\mathrm{Representation}_S(\\sigma,M,V_\\sigma)\\land\\pi=\\{f\\in V_\\sigma^G:\\operatorname{Smooth}(f)\\land\\forall m\\in M\\;\\forall n\\in N\\;\\forall g\\in G\\;(f(mng)=\\delta_P(m)^{1/2}\\sigma(m)f(g))\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Parabolic induction: induce from parabolic subgroup; builds representations of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"G\">\\(G\\)</span></li>\n<li>Levi: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M\">\\(M\\)</span> is Levi factor of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P = MN\">\\(P = MN\\)</span>; modular character <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\delta_P\">\\(\\delta_P\\)</span> corrects Haar</li>\n<li>The factor <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\delta_P^{1/2}\">\\(\\delta_P^{1/2}\\)</span> makes this the normalized induction; omitting it gives unnormalized induction.</li>\n<li>Langlands classification: irreducible reps of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"G\">\\(G\\)</span> are irreducible subquotients of induced representations</li>\n<li>The Jacquet functor, rather than the ordinary restriction <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\pi|_M\">\\(\\pi|_M\\)</span>, is adjoint to parabolic induction (with the side depending on normalization conventions).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Bushnell and Henniart, The Local Langlands Conjecture for GL(2)</li>\n<li>Borel and Wallach, Continuous Cohomology of Discrete Groups</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch08/58-df-reductive-group.md","status":"resolved","id":"8790321df936a708","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch08/58-df-reductive-group.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch12/58-df-representation.md","status":"resolved","id":"6f58babd1e46f709","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-df-representation.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch08/58-df-reductive-group.md","status":"resolved","id":"8790321df936a708","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{Reductive}$ (reductive-group predicate, see [[../batch08/58-df-reductive-group.md]])","embed":false},{"target":"../batch12/58-df-representation.md","status":"resolved","id":"6f58babd1e46f709","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Representation}_S$ (representation predicate, see [[../batch12/58-df-representation.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"G,P,M,N,\\sigma,V_\\sigma,\\pi\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"P=M\\ltimes N","display":false},{"tex":"M","display":false},{"tex":"N","display":false},{"tex":"\\delta_P","display":false},{"tex":"P","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Reductive}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Representation}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ParabolicInduction}_S\\subseteq V^4","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}parabolic\\text{-}induction} \\vdash \\mathrm{ParabolicInduction}_S(\\pi,G,P,\\sigma)\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{Reductive}(G)\\land P=M\\ltimes N\\land\\mathrm{Representation}_S(\\sigma,M,V_\\sigma)\\land\\pi=\\{f\\in V_\\sigma^G:\\operatorname{Smooth}(f)\\land\\forall m\\in M\\;\\forall n\\in N\\;\\forall g\\in G\\;(f(mng)=\\delta_P(m)^{1/2}\\sigma(m)f(g))\\}","display":true},{"tex":"G","display":false},{"tex":"M","display":false},{"tex":"P = MN","display":false},{"tex":"\\delta_P","display":false},{"tex":"\\delta_P^{1/2}","display":false},{"tex":"G","display":false},{"tex":"\\pi|_M","display":false}],"bytes":1958,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-937","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-parabolic-induction.md|58-df-parabolic-induction]]（batch13）"}],"outgoing":["8790321df936a708","6f58babd1e46f709"]}